What pair is printed by this C program? The && operator short-circuits and sequences evaluation of its left operand before its right operand.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main(void) {
    int a[5] = {1,2,0,4,5};
    int i = 0, sum = 0;
    while (i < 5 && a[i++] > 0)
        sum += a[i];
    printf("%d %d\n", i, sum);
    return 0;
}
```

